      "side": 1,
      "message": "To collect syshealth data while VM is running, I gathered data about CPU time(user/nice/sys/idle) and memory size(total/free/available/buffer/cached) information for every second. For designing atom with more detailed structure and complete implementation, I have some questions below.\n\n1. Does the data looks enough for measuring syshealth in Microdroid? I\u0027m worrying if I have something missing which is really important. For example, I saw PSS was appeared in so many charts in go/avf-data.\n\n2. As I gather data for every second, the data size would be extremely large. So I\u0027ll aggregate with VALUE metric, and get a representable data like MAX/MIN/AVG/SUM value of each field. And the data will be classified by `uid/package_name` and `vm_identifier`. Does it sound good?",
      "revId": "5fffec1c6a88b6a3788853f74e7b7ef6f8eb177d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
